<title>USA: Washington Homes Q3 net loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Washington Homes Q3 net loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>LANDOVER, Md. 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr	   loss	 $2.12   profit	 $0.08</p>
<p> Net	   loss	16,834   profit	   614</p>
<p> Revs			42,801		   39,404</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   7,943		    7,943</p>
<p>	   9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr	   loss	 $1.92   profit	 $0.22</p>
<p> Net	   loss	15,249   profit	 1,709</p>
<p> Revs		     138,143		  112,113</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   7,943		    7,943</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Washington Homes Inc said its third quarter period ended April 30.</p>
<p>Net income for the third quarter and first nine months of 1997 included a loss of $16.2 million net of tax effect, or $2.04 per share, associated with a previously announced write-down of goodwill and land inventory and an extraordinary loss from a previously announced tax settlement with the Internal Revenue Service.</p>
